<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
		<ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
		<Nullable>enable</Nullable>
		<Authors>LostBeard</Authors>
		<RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE.txt</PackageLicenseFile>
		<PackageIcon>icon-128.png</PackageIcon>
		<GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
		<!-- 🔴 With this on, `dotnet BUILD -c Release` makes the nupkg. `dotnet pack` does NOT rebuild: it repackages the last
		     build's DLL, so a version bump never reaches the binary (2026-11-01: 1.4.0-local.5 shipped a DLL stamped
		     1.4.0-local.4+1cc937c). Build, then check the packed DLL's InformationalVersion. -->
		<GeneratePackageOnBuild>True</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
		<EmbedAllSources>true</EmbedAllSources>
		<DebugType>Embedded</DebugType>
		<LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
		<IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/LostBeard/SpawnDev.AI</PackageProjectUrl>
		<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/LostBeard/SpawnDev.AI.git</RepositoryUrl>
		<PackageTags>AI;LLM;Ollama;DotNetWebAssembly;WebGPU;GGUF;ToolCalling</PackageTags>
		<Title>SpawnDev.AI.Server</Title>
		<Version>1.4.0-local.7</Version>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>v1.4.0 - AiFaceEngine: face detection and recognition (YuNet + SFace) on the shared accelerator, with a face registry (introductions, Visitor N guests, expiry). On SpawnDev.ILGPU.ML 5.8.0 and SpawnDev.ILGPU 5.4.14. v1.3.0 - Live words: AiStreamingSpeechEngine (Nemotron Speech Streaming 0.6B, words as they are spoken, 5.63% WER on 60 LibriSpeech clips, a 160 ms chunk in ~70 ms). Full history: CHANGELOG.md</PackageReleaseNotes>
		<Description>Ollama/OpenAI-compatible model server on the SpawnDev.ILGPU.ML inference engine (GGUF, KV-cache decode, WebGPU dispatch-plan capture/replay). One handler core, two transports: HTTP on desktop (drop-in for Ollama clients on :11434), MessagePort in the browser (shared/dedicated worker) - the same request/response shapes either way.</Description>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<ProjectReference Include="..\SpawnDev.AI\SpawnDev.AI.csproj" />
	</ItemGroup>
	
	<ItemGroup>
		<None Include="..\icon-128.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
		<None Include="..\LICENSE.txt" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
		<None Include="..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<PackageReference Include="SpawnDev.ILGPU.ML" Version="5.8.1-local.2" />
		<!-- Direct reference: NuGet resolves the LOWEST version satisfying ML's floor (5.3.4 asks for
		     SpawnDev.ILGPU >= 5.3.5), so an ILGPU fix released after the ML package reaches the server and the
		     demo only through this line. Keep it at the newest ILGPU. -->
		<PackageReference Include="SpawnDev.ILGPU" Version="5.4.15-local.2" />
		<PackageReference Include="SpawnDev.SpawnJS.WebWorkers" Version="2.2.5" />
	</ItemGroup>

</Project>
